;; THE SUPERVISOR'S OWN WORKFLOW — a stream beside the run, not a node in it.
;;
;; The run being supervised has its own manifest and its own context. This is
;; the second one: the supervisor's. They share a run id and nothing else, and
;; that is the point — a supervisor whose context is the implementer's context
;; is reading the work instead of watching the worker.
;;
;; One pass of this manifest is one look at the run: gather what has happened,
;; decide whether anything needs saying or changing, then act — steer the run
;; through the interventions queue, tune the harness through the mutation
;; protocol, or do neither, which is the common and correct answer.
;;
;; The stream driver (samizdat.agent.oversight) decides WHEN a pass happens.
;; This decides what a pass IS, so both halves stay editable at runtime.
{:description "The supervisor's parallel stream: one pass gathers the run's health, reasons about it as the supervisor role, and applies whatever it decided — a steer into the running run, a tuning change for the next one, or nothing. Runs beside a run rather than inside it, so a stalled implementer cannot starve it."

 :input-schema
 ;; :oversight/carry is the supervisor's branch from the previous pass, so
 ;; the stream continues one conversation rather than starting a new one each
 ;; time. Absent on the first pass, and nil on any pass that stayed quiet.
 [:map [:oversight/carry {:optional true} :any]]

 :cells {:start   :oversight/gather
         :reason  :oversight/reason
         :apply   :oversight/apply
         :quiet   :oversight/quiet}

 :edges {:start  {:reason :reason
                  ;; Nothing worth a model call. By far the most common
                  ;; outcome, and the cheap path has to be the default or the
                  ;; stream costs more than the run it watches.
                  :quiet  :quiet}
         :reason :apply
         :apply  :end
         :quiet  :end}

 :dispatches {:start [[:reason {:oversight/worth-a-look? true}]
                      [:quiet  _]]}

 :invariants
 [{:type :must-follow :if :reason :then :apply :enforced true
   :protects "A pass that reasoned always reaches apply. A supervisor that
              decides something and then drops it on the floor is worse than
              one that never ran: the decision is in the journal, so the record
              shows a steer that never happened."}

  {:type :must-precede :cell :start :before :reason :enforced true
   :protects "The supervisor reasons over gathered evidence, never over an
              empty data map. Its whole authority to change the harness rests
              on having looked first."}]}
